schema: concept-lineage
object:
  title: Stablecoins
  type: concept-lineage
  short_description: >-
    Cryptocurrencies pegged to a stable reference asset (typically the US
    dollar) so their value doesn't swing the way bitcoin's does, making them
    practical for organizations needing predictable budgets.
  source_traditions:
    - crypto/DeFi
    - traditional finance (currency-peg concept)
  toolkit_usage: >-
    Positioned in this article as the practical, everyday-operations use case
    for nonprofits (vs. bitcoin/volatile-crypto donations for one-off crisis
    fundraising) — cross-border payments and predictable budgeting.
  adjacent_meanings:
    - crypto-donations
    - cross-border-payments
  important_distinctions:
    - >-
      stablecoins-vs-volatile-crypto — stablecoins are framed as suited to
      recurring operational use, not speculative holding
  risks_of_flattening: >-
    The article doesn't distinguish stablecoin types (fiat-collateralized vs.
    algorithmic vs. crypto-collateralized) or their differing risk profiles —
    treating "stablecoin" as a single practical mechanism.
  maturity: raw
  ai_assisted: true
  provenance:
    origin: src/content/docs/case-studies-nonprofits.md
    transformation: summarized
    authorship: ai-assisted
